cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ORM query performance across four database systems: public code and measurements"
abstract: >-
  Public artifact for How Portable Is ORM Query Performance? Evidence from Four
  Database Systems. Includes Django and SQLAlchemy query implementations,
  measurement harnesses, and reproducible analysis of PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle
  and Commercial System A. The revision campaign rc20261008 (October 2026)
  re-measures the scale-factor-1 analytical grid under a frozen protocol, with
  matched transactions, scale factor 2, a separate client, a second server, a
  four-path decomposition and censored-cell validation; its per-call records,
  protocols, environment inventories and measured source are released. The
  September 2026 measurements are retained as the historical comparison.
  Commercial System A uses an anonymous label. The manuscript is not yet
  published.
